From 3408ce54537503391acc69e80c776181089ecf5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antony Alexin <antonyalexin2604@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 06:04:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: IMM stressed vol recalibration + per-asset GFC
 calibration (CRE51.15/CRE53)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fix A (CRE51.15): run_batch_portfolios stressed EAD now uses _eepe_one_year()
  instead of eee.mean() — enforces one-year EEPE window for stress scenarios
  as required by CRE53 §EEPE, consistent with compute_exposure_profile().

Fix B (CRE53 stress calibration): Replace single 2×base shortcut in MarketParams
  with per-asset-class GFC 2007-09 empirically-calibrated stressed volatilities:
    EQ  stressed_vol:       0.40 → 0.38  (S&P 500 realized ~38%)
    FX  fx_stressed_vol:    0.40 → 0.18  (major pair realized ~18%)
    IR  ir_stressed_vol:    0.030 → 0.020 (10Y UST σ_r ~120-200bp/yr)
    CR  cr_stressed_vol:    zero → 0.65  (IG CDX log-vol; was else→zeros BUG)
    CMDTY cmdty_stressed_vol: 0.40 → 0.58 (WTI realized ~58%/yr)

  simulate_netting_set() now routes each asset class to its own vol pair
  (base + stressed) instead of the single self.p.stressed_vol for EQ/FX/CMDTY.

  CR exposure fixed: CDS/TRS previously fell to else-branch → zero MTM.
  Now modelled via GBM on spread level with s₀=90bp IG reference and
  DV01-approximate duration scaling, consistent with market_state CDS formula.

  validate() extended to check all five asset-class vol pairs and assert
  stressed_vol >= base_vol for every class.

  config.py: GFCStressConfig dataclass added — documents source, window,
  and annualised values for each asset class.

Quantitative impact (5-trade portfolio: IR 50M + FX 30M + EQ 20M + CR 25M + CMDTY 10M):
  EAD regulatory BEFORE: USD 7,999,731  (1.88× SA-CCR)
  EAD regulatory AFTER:  USD 5,653,488  (1.33× SA-CCR)
  Reduction: -USD 2,346,243 (-29.3%)

  Primary drivers:
    FX:  40% → 18% stressed vol (largest single contributor to reduction)
    IR:  3.0% → 2.0% stressed vol
    CR:  zero → 65% stressed vol WITH s₀=90bp scaling (net positive but bounded)
    CMDTY: 40% → 58% (partially offsets reductions)

Tests: 47/47 regulatory fix tests pass; all MC/engine tests pass
