From 3c19d984f9b350fa772a4b2f134c215afe27edce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antony Alexin <antonyalexin2604@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 06:39:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: enforce GFC stressed vol floors +
 max(current,stressed) EAD (CRE53/CRE51.15)

Fix 1  (CRE51.15): EAD_regulatory = max(current EAD, stressed EAD)
       compute_rwa(), run_for_portfolio(), run_batch_portfolios() all confirmed active.

Fix B  (CRE53 stress calibration): GFC empirical floors enforced at three layers
       Layer 1 - MarketParams defaults: EQ=0.38, IR=0.020, FX=0.18, CR=0.65, CMDTY=0.58
       Layer 2 - apply_to_imm(): max(rolling, 1.5x base, GFC floor) for all 5 asset classes
       Layer 3 - calibration_cache.json updated to embed GFC floor values

Root cause fixed: apply_to_imm() was overwriting GFC-calibrated stressed vols
with rolling 1yr window estimates (2x base shortcut), silently undoing MarketParams.
The calibration window cannot span 2007-09 and always underestimates stress.

Quantitative impact:
  IMM/SA-CCR ratio: 1.916x (before) -> 1.402x (after)
  EAD stressed:     .16M -> .97M (-26.8%)

Tests: 7 new TestGFCVolCalibration tests added; 207/207 total passing
